[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:example ;
    owl:annotatedSource sosa:Procedure ;
    owl:annotatedTarget "The measured wind speed differs depending on the height of the sensor above the surface, e.g., due to friction. Consequently, procedures for measuring wind speed define a standard height for anemometers above ground, typically 10m for meteorological measures and 2m in Agrometeorology. This definition of height, sensor placement, and so forth are defined by the Procedure."@en ;
    sk:role "Inference" .

